/**
 * Determines the optimal position to wrap a given text string based on a specified maximum width.
 * This method is primarily used for text formatting, such as in help messages, to ensure lines do
 * not exceed a visual width limit. It prioritizes wrapping at explicit line breaks ('\n', '\t'),
 * then at whitespace characters (' ', '\n', '\r') before or at the maximum wrap position.
 * If no suitable natural wrap point is found within the width, it attempts to find the next
 * word boundary after the maximum width, potentially resulting in a line longer than the specified width.
