 *         If 'F' or 'D' parsing fails due to range/precision, {@code BigDecimal} is attempted as a fallback.</li>
 *     <li>For numbers without an explicit type suffix:
 *         <ul>
 *             <li>If it appears to be an integer (no decimal, no exponent), it tries {@code Integer}, then {@code Long}, then {@code BigInteger}.</li>
 *             <li>If it appears to be a floating-point number (has decimal or exponent), it tries {@code Float}, then {@code Double}, then {@code BigDecimal}.</li>
