6.  `int i = start + 2;` so `i = 2`.
7.  `if (i == sz)`: `2 == 2` is `true`.
8.  `return false;` (correctly rejects "0x").

Consider `str = "0xG"`.
1.  `sz = 3`. `start = 0`.
2.  `if (sz > start + 1)`: `3 > 1` is `true`.
3.  `if (chars[start] == '0' && chars[start + 1] == 'x')`: `true`.
4.  `int i = start + 2;` so `i = 2`.
